  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Nardostachin may interact with the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14 through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links Nardostachin to Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, which is targeted by 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol. This compound, in turn, targets the 26S proteasome subunit, indicating a chain of interactions where Nardostachin may influence the activity of the proteasome through its effect on demethylase activity. The second and third pathways show that Nardostachin also targets Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which is targeted by Cassialactone and Lethedioside B, both of which also target the 26S proteasome subunit. These findings suggest that Nardostachin may exert its effects on the proteasome through different molecular mechanisms, possibly involving the modulation of protein targets that regulate proteasome function. The evidence is consistent across multiple pathways, but the exact nature of the interaction remains uncertain due to the complexity of the signaling networks involved."
